WEBVTT

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.860
MOBILE SUIT
<b>GUNDAM
VICTORY</b>

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:32.160
Aboard the League Militaire's new flagship, the Jeanne d'Arc,

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.830
was Hangerg Ewin, Üso's father.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:39.430
Even as Üso told him of his mother's death,

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:42.500
he was shaken by how much his father had changed.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:50.330
But, when pressed by Pippiniden's space fleet,

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:55.060
Üso showed his father just how much he'd grown,

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:57.430
and gained his attention.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:00.530
A SHINING VORTEX OF FRESH BLOOD

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:04.260
"A Shining Vortex of Fresh Blood".

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.360
Trying to crush me with your shields?!

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:19.500
I was saved. By who?! Odelo and Tomáš?

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.160
They're still watching my back!

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.430
That's amazing!

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:29.030
Üso, I'm taking those points for my score!

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:34.560
But, Üso, aren't you going a little overboard with your dad watching?

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:36.360
Going overboard?

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:40.260
That's not what's got me so worked up.

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:44.330
Unless I try my best as a pilot, Dad will yell at me!

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:55.630
A formidable fleet.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:58.060
They've penetrated our first defense line!

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:01.460
Captain Tassilo's Shubaten doesn't seem to be moving yet.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:02.530
So it would seem.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:06.200
His ships are gathered aft at combat range four.

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:09.260
He won't move till we ask for help?

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:12.500
Fall back to the second defense line!

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:21.530
The enemy fleet's falling back!

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:24.030
Odelo! Tomáš! Do you know about this?

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:25.460
How would they?

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.800
BESPA still has many other fleets!

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:29.930
If they rendezvous, it'll be a pain!

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.660
They've laid blinder mines!

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:39.800
Üso, that's enough.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.960
We've pushed them back far enough.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.130
Let's retreat.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.200
But...

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:47.460
There's another fleet behind the Rasteo Fleet.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:51.830
It appears to be the unit with that saucer-riding mobile suit.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.400
That huge mobile suit on the saucer?

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:58.860
The mobile suit that may have been making those bell noises.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:03.530
And behind that is that ring they call Angel Halo.

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:08.560
Still, why did the fleet that came at us first retreat so quickly?

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:11.230
They saw how many of us are here and panicked.

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:12.260
Right.

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:15.230
If that's the case, it'll just get harder from here on in.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:18.800
They'll send more fleets from Angel Halo, right?

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:21.930
The bells seem to be coming from there.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:26.160
But Karl's quiet. Why is that?

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:30.200
Those bells...

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.730
They seem different than the ones we heard on Earth.

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:37.900
They seem to be trying to scare people, to tempt them.

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:39.300
You still hear them?

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:41.960
It's not exactly like hearing them.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:44.660
I know in my head that they're there.

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:49.700
We don't hear them unless we see that thing on the saucer, right?

00:04:49.730 --> 00:04:51.600
Yeah, we don't hear them.

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:01.560
Where's Commandant Pippiniden?

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:03.000
How should I know?

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:05.330
Does that mean he's in his quarters?

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:07.160
What was that?

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:11.600
Ever since I escaped the guillotine, I've come to fear his voice.

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:12.630
But...

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:15.830
He never told you about Angel Halo.

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:19.130
You must have questions about Kagatie's methods, surely!

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:22.630
I do, but to just keep sending me in front again and again is...

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:25.000
After the ceasefire was signed,

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:28.230
you and Cronicle abandoned Operation Earth Clean...

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.060
...and returned to space.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.060
That was pure egotism!

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:34.360
Who's that strange woman there?

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:38.360
How do you do, Captain? I'm Lupe Cineau.

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:41.660
We have refreshment time before the next mission, right?

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:44.260
Are you saying you won't give me any backup?!

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.160
I didn't say that!

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:51.030
As I just said, we're reinforcing Angel Halo's defense deployment.

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:55.130
Which just boils down to you using us as a shield!

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:56.960
Ms. Lupe Cineau.

00:05:57.130 --> 00:06:00.630
What's wrong? I'm wearing it over my pilot suit.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:01.530
Still...

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:02.930
You like it, don't you?

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.600
In another time and place.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:07.200
Are Tassilo and Kagatie plotting something?

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.700
That thing with the guillotine was a sham!

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:14.160
To hide Angel Halo's existence from the Zanscare people...

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:17.200
...and even us in the Motorad Fleet.

00:06:18.130 --> 00:06:20.060
I've heard that, once it's complete,

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:22.960
it will become a gigantic brainwave transmitter.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:26.500
If they plan to use it to mentally control humanity,

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:27.960
we should use it ourselves.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:30.260
To control everyone from Kagatie on down?

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:32.600
I like it!

00:06:32.630 --> 00:06:35.360
Call the captain. Let's polish our strategy.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:36.660
Roger.

00:06:51.230 --> 00:06:53.630
Captain, I heard your discussion.

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:56.500
Should we let Pippiniden do as he likes, hm?

00:06:56.530 --> 00:06:59.260
What can some upstart pilot accomplish?

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.930
If he's planning to go after me,

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:05.460
then just have him attack the League Militaire Fleet.

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:06.930
That's right.

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:10.400
Or perhaps I should attack Pippiniden myself.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:16.230
We will meet the Federation Forces' advance,

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:19.260
then fall back to the Shubaten Fleet's position.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.300
If we do that, even Tassilo will act!

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.900
But, they'll send out that Zanneck, as well.

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:26.960
I'll attack it from behind.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:30.100
And if we can draw that white suit in, as well...

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:31.360
What fun we'll have.

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:34.560
Even someone as hard to kill as Tassilo will be sunk, right?

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:40.830
How about you wear a new dress that I like?

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.900
What gives you the right to say that?

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:45.800
The right of a man's relationship with a woman.

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:49.330
As soon as you show me you can win the war.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.860
I want to be kissed by a young man!

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:57.960
So much work to get a man to take things seriously!

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:01.660
Looks like it's finished.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:10.400
The Birknau, Pippiniden's personal use command mobile armor.

00:08:10.700 --> 00:08:12.200
It should come in handy.

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:17.000
Life would have been easier if he'd just stayed a pilot.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:18.960
Attach missile pods!

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:30.630
All I want is a genuine fight to see how strong or weak a person is.

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:34.560
A Newtype can understand that, right Boy?

00:08:38.630 --> 00:08:40.730
We'll hit their first defense line...

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:42.660
...before the enemy fleets can rendezvous.

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:45.500
After the mobile suits launch, all ships, move in!

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:47.630
Don't get hit by our own beams!

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:52.260
Shrike Team 1, Hexa, Cony Francis, here I go!

00:08:55.230 --> 00:08:57.900
Unit 2, Hexa, Miliera Katan, moving out!

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:05.030
A new model of beam shield? Why am I getting it now?

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:07.530
Calibrating the output device took a while.

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:08.730
It'll work, right?

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:12.430
Perfectly! Just be careful you don't go crazy with the power.

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:14.130
Roger, I'll try.

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:19.630
Shrike Team 5, Francesca Ohara, here I go!

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:28.530
The main Federation forces are moving out in front this time,

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:32.500
so I think we'll have to take care of that saucer suit.

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:33.900
Understood.

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:36.900
Üso wants to try his clothesline pole on it.

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:39.930
I recall saying I'd let you handle it, Miss Juca!

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:42.030
You can let me handle it!

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:43.230
Right, Üso.

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:47.500
Don't run off to fight alone just because V2 is so powerful!

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:50.060
Understood. I've got Haro here with me, too.

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:50.830
Haro!

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:52.330
V2, moving out!

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:59.200
Don't be in too much of a rush, okay?

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:02.960
Don't be lured in by those bells, Üso.

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:08.660
I won't be afraid.

00:10:09.230 --> 00:10:12.760
Because my father is watching to see how I fight!

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:17.060
BESPA is stubborn!

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:19.360
But we're pushing them back!

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:22.700
Fall! Fall!

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:29.460
We can't get to the Rasteo?

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:30.730
What?

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:38.630
You saved me, Üso!

00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:40.560
He's using the tire?

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:46.130
If I try following him, we can sneak into the middle of the enemy!

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:50.400
We are being pursued by a mediocre enemy, Üso!

00:10:50.430 --> 00:10:52.130
Is that Tomáš?

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:55.560
If I can just keep going and get close to the Motorad Fleet...!

00:10:56.430 --> 00:10:59.030
The bells. Where are they?

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:05.230
It's not coming from the Motorad ship Rasteo that's in front of me.

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:06.700
It's further back.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:09.460
Angel Halo!

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:14.630
Tomáš! Odelo and Miss Juca are...

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:35.430
Miss Marbet, it's definitely coming from that direction!

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:37.160
No doubt about it!

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:38.760
Get to the room below!

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:41.460
Tell me if anything else unusual happens to Karl!

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:42.300
Right!

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:46.430
There, there. I know you're scared of the bells.

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:48.500
They'll quiet down soon.

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:52.130
We're late!

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:53.800
Warren, give them missile support!

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:54.630
Right!

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:56.360
Are you okay?

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:58.130
Here.

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:03.700
Karl, it's okay.

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:07.230
Drink your milk, and the bells will go away.

00:12:09.730 --> 00:12:10.930
There we go.

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:13.300
Strap him down in the meantime.

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:14.360
Right.

00:12:15.030 --> 00:12:17.100
Do you want a mama too, Flanders?

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:22.600
Now they're coming in from 2 o'clock, Sis!

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:25.500
Lens catch! Miss Marbet, retreat toward the front!

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:26.000
Karel!

00:12:26.030 --> 00:12:26.730
Roger!

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:31.160
Amazing. Coming back into space has sharpened our senses!

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:32.330
No.

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:35.300
We're probably just getting drawn into this.

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:36.960
Drawn into it?

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:40.400
Besides that, there's a warmth here, now.

00:12:40.430 --> 00:12:43.900
A warmth we felt on Earth, from the land and trees.

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:45.600
Sis is right.

00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:49.930
Karlmann laughing and crying isn't just from him being afraid.

00:12:50.030 --> 00:12:52.930
In space, where you can feel the warmth of the land and trees,

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:54.830
Üso and the others are fighting?

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:57.300
Maybe they're on to something.

00:12:57.430 --> 00:13:00.000
I don't feel it.

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:03.630
But I know that it's true.

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:09.330
That's three. Incoming!

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:16.000
This shield's power is making me overheat!

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:22.460
Is that what he meant by the shield having such high output?

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:26.660
They got my main monitor!

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:29.260
And my manipulators are down!

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:36.130
What just blew?!

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:38.330
Looks like it was one of Shrike Team's Hexas!

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:39.460
Whose machine?

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:53.360
A brand new model, and I hardly got to use it.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:57.700
The Hexa is based on the Victory.

00:13:58.130 --> 00:13:59.930
It wasn't the machine's fault.

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:03.300
In the end, I just didn't have the power.

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:07.930
Will that kid be able to use it? Üso...

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:26.760
Why am I not afraid?

00:14:27.960 --> 00:14:30.400
Because I can feel Üso's presence, now?

00:14:32.730 --> 00:14:33.860
It's pretty.

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:38.900
I can last another hour.

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:57.430
Odelo from the White Ark.

00:14:57.930 --> 00:15:00.930
Miss Frannie? Do you have enough air?

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:02.500
I... I'm fine!

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:03.900
You aren't hurt?

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:08.030
Don't worry about me! Take this shield to V2!

00:15:08.230 --> 00:15:09.960
The one behind you?

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:12.930
The output of the mega beam shield is too high!

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:14.860
The Hexa can't handle it!

00:15:15.730 --> 00:15:17.100
Get the enemy ship!

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:21.260
One ship, destroyed! What?!

00:15:21.300 --> 00:15:23.560
Enemy! Enemy! Enemy!

00:15:26.430 --> 00:15:27.930
I've found you, Boy!

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:31.000
This is for biting my breast!

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:44.330
What?!

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:46.530
He severed the Einerad rings?!

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:50.300
Üso, are you okay?

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:53.530
They got the mega beam rifle, but let's charge in anyway!

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:55.700
Because Cony and the others are headed forward!

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:56.430
Right!

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:02.430
Vessel 1 has been hit! Withdrawing from the battle line!

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:03.700
All right, Captain.

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:06.760
This should draw the Shubaten Fleet into the battle, as well.

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:09.930
Yes. We're entering combat range, right on schedule.

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:11.400
You have the conn!

00:16:11.430 --> 00:16:12.800
You're launching, sir?

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:16.160
A man who just polishes his seat with his ass is finished!

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:26.860
We need to deploy, don't we?

00:16:27.100 --> 00:16:29.730
We're now within firing range of the enemy's guns.

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:32.930
No, Pippiniden still has power left to him.

00:16:33.060 --> 00:16:35.700
If we don't have him exhaust it, it'll be dangerous.

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:43.230
We're pushing them back quickly.

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:46.660
That's also due to your son's great work.

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:47.500
No, sir.

00:16:48.030 --> 00:16:50.500
It's because the enemy's vanguard, the Rasteo Fleet,

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:53.700
is in such a hurry to rendezvous with the fleet to its rear.

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:55.700
It's not just that.

00:16:55.930 --> 00:16:58.460
You should acknowledge your son's strength.

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:01.060
Thank you very much, but...

00:17:02.530 --> 00:17:05.360
It's painful to think of my son as being someone so powerful.

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:06.830
It's like he's a stranger.

00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:10.060
A child will eventually surpass his parent.

00:17:10.100 --> 00:17:13.860
But I suppose you don't want to see it happening before your eyes.

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:17.900
The fleet further to the rear...

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:20.930
...of that backline fleet is Angel Halo, right?

00:17:20.960 --> 00:17:22.400
I can see the layout, now.

00:17:22.660 --> 00:17:24.930
Shahkti, how's Karl doing?

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:26.900
He's been happy since that last time.

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:31.830
But, it's like I keep hearing the bells in the distance.

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:34.500
Really? Any mobile suits nearby?

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:35.460
None.

00:17:37.730 --> 00:17:39.700
Where did Üso and the others go?!

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.830
Attack the white suit from the left and right!

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:52.060
I'll finish him from the front!

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:52.500
Right!

00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:53.060
Right!

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:05.000
Oh, no!

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:05.960
Haro!

00:18:06.430 --> 00:18:08.730
We tricked you, Boy!

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:11.630
Say your prayers!

00:18:11.660 --> 00:18:12.700
Not yet!

00:18:13.930 --> 00:18:15.000
I can't move!

00:18:20.360 --> 00:18:24.600
Much as I'd like to praise you, come sleep in my bosom!

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:25.560
What?!

00:18:30.430 --> 00:18:32.260
You've no place to run, Boy!

00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:35.300
At last, I will achieve my dream!

00:18:35.400 --> 00:18:36.830
I'm your dream, Miss Lupe?!

00:18:36.860 --> 00:18:40.930
Yes! To be purified by a boy who has worked so hard!

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:42.800
That is my dream!

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:44.000
Open your eyes!

00:18:46.300 --> 00:18:47.330
You still...

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:49.630
Miss Juca! What?!

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:57.160
That's why, with you at my breast, I will make you mine!

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:04.400
I won't... I won't be your dream!

00:19:04.730 --> 00:19:06.960
I'm nobody's tool!

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:16.160
